<Base title="Governance & Transparency" description="GEAR Moto Foundation governance principles, proposed legal structure, independent oversight, and the future publication of verified corporate filings and bylaws.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Accountability / Riders Helping Riders</div><h1>TRUST IS BUILT.<br/><span class="accent">NOT ASSUMED.</span></h1><p class="lede" style="color:#e5e8eb">Transparent decisions. Responsible stewardship. Support for every rider who qualifies.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
<div class="program-callout"><strong>Formation and document status:</strong> This page describes our developing governance approach. Official Utah incorporation, adopted bylaws, and IRS status have not yet been independently verified for publication here. A working draft is not a filed or adopted document.</div>
<h2>Founder-Led. Board-Governed. Professionally Operated.</h2>
<p>GEAR is being developed as a Utah nonprofit public charity with no voting membership. The planned independent Board of Directors would provide fiduciary oversight, approve core policies and budgets, and review conflicts. The Founder, President &amp; Executive Director would lead day-to-day operations subject to the Articles, bylaws, approved policies, and applicable law. The proposed five-director Board includes the Founder and four independent directors. The Founder may serve as Interim Board Chair during startup; a qualified independent Chair would later be elected from among the independent directors. Every lawfully seated director has one ordinary vote, subject to applicable conflict-of-interest and voting rules.</p>
<p>The foundation's mission spans <strong>Gear, Education, Assistance, and Recovery</strong>. Charitable assistance is designed for eligible members of an open-ended rider community, not selected friends, clubs, sponsors, directors, or donors.</p>
<section class="gov-library" aria-labelledby="gov-library-heading">
<div class="gov-library-heading"><div><span class="gov-overline">DOCUMENT LIBRARY / ORGANIZATIONAL TRANSPARENCY</span><h2 id="gov-library-heading">Our Governing Documents</h2></div><p>Our commitment to accountability includes making the documents that govern GEAR accessible to the community. As formation progresses, verified and formally adopted documents will be available here to read and download.</p></div>
<div class="gov-document-notice"><strong>Current status — organizational development.</strong> These document categories reflect our planned governance and reporting commitments. Draft documents are under review and are not official corporate records. We will publish approved copies only after the relevant filing, adoption or authorization has been verified.</div>
<div class="gov-documents">
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</div><span>LEGAL FORMATION</span><h3>Articles of Incorporation</h3><p>GEAR's formal Utah corporate formation document, including its charitable purpose and governing provisions. The filed version will be published after acceptance and verification.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Pending filing verification</strong><small>Official PDF forthcoming</small></div></article>
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</div><span>BOARD GOVERNANCE</span><h3>Corporate Bylaws</h3><p>How GEAR's Board is organized and how directors, officers, meetings, voting, leadership succession and fiduciary oversight are governed.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Counsel-review draft</strong><small>Adopted PDF forthcoming</small></div></article>
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</div><span>ETHICS &amp; OVERSIGHT</span><h3>Conflict of Interest Policy</h3><p>Safeguards for identifying conflicts, recording disclosures and ensuring disinterested review of compensation and related-party transactions.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Draft policy</strong><small>Approved PDF forthcoming</small></div></article>
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">04</div><span>RIDER SUPPORT</span><h3>Rider Relief Policy</h3><p>Proposed eligibility, confidential review, approval controls and responsible limits for accident-related medical assistance. Applications and awards are not open.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Draft policy</strong><small>Adopted PDF forthcoming</small></div></article>
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">05</div><span>LEADERSHIP</span><h3>Board &amp; Leadership</h3><p>Meet GEAR's founder and learn about the planned independent Board, leadership responsibilities and current governance stage.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Public information available</strong><a href="/leadership/">View leadership <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>
<article><div class="gov-doc-icon" aria-hidden="true">06</div><span>TAX &amp; TRANSPARENCY</span><h3>IRS &amp; Financial Reports</h3><p>When issued and verified, we intend to share applicable IRS determination information, required public returns and accountable financial reporting.</p><div class="gov-doc-bottom"><strong>Not yet available</strong><small>Verified reports forthcoming</small></div></article>
</div>
<p class="gov-library-footnote">Availability and publication dates depend on formal legal actions and verification. Working board packets, confidential director disclosures, sensitive applicant data and internal planning records are not part of the public document library.</p>
</section>
<h2>Accountability Commitments</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Independent oversight:</strong> Disinterested directors would evaluate founder compensation, related-party transactions, and other potential conflicts through documented procedures.</li>
<li><strong>Fair awards:</strong> Grant decisions would depend on approved eligibility, need, funding limits and conflict recusals—not membership, friendship, or donated amounts.</li>
<li><strong>Stewardship:</strong> Program-restricted donations would be used for their intended charitable purposes; no donor would designate an individual beneficiary.</li>
<li><strong>Rider privacy:</strong> Medical and financial records would require approved, confidential application channels, not general email.</li>
<li><strong>Truthful reporting:</strong> Planned outcomes and illustrative photographs would never be presented as completed grant or service results.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Where We Are Today</h2><p>Official document publication requires independent confirmation of the filed Utah Articles, legal review of founder-protection provisions and current law, adoption of bylaws and policies, and verification of appropriate registrations and federal status. The pending governance documents will not be displayed as though they are final.</p>
